      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Essential Documentation &amp; Insurance for Seamless Gurgaon‑Mumbai Vehicle Moves</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">When planning a cross-city relocation, particularly from Mumbai to Gurgaon, it is essential to familiarize yourself with the various documents and insurance requirements involved. These preparations will ensure a smooth and hassle-free moving process. In this guide, we will discuss the necessary documents and the importance of marine transit insurance for your belongings during the move. Additionally, we will highlight the primary keyword "packers and movers Mumbai to Gurgaon" for your convenience.

1. E-Way Bill:

The e-Way Bill is a document generated electronically under the GST (Goods and Services Tax) system in India. It is mandatory for inter-state transportation of goods exceeding certain value limits (Rs. 50,000 for certain states like Delhi, Gujarat, and Haryana). The e-Way Bill serves as proof of the goods' movement and helps track them during transportation.

